Scope
-----
The project license covers original HTMLCut software and project-authored
associated documentation, configuration and synthetic test/evaluation fixtures.
Vendored material under patches/ retains its upstream license expressions and
notices. It is not relicensed by the project license declaration.

The API baseline under semver-baseline/ is retained source from the published
release identified by its BASELINE.toml. It retains that release's license.
In source distributions, the earlier project MIT text is in
LICENSES/HTMLCut-published-MIT.txt; that text
records the published grant and is not an MIT alternative for newly covered
v18 source. Earlier published tags and release artifacts retain their terms.

The project license does not purport to license caller-provided HTML, captured
third-party pages or extracted source content. Rights to that content remain
with the applicable rights holders.

Source availability and third-party terms
----------------------------------------
Matching HTMLCut source is available from the source archives on the same
GitHub release and the exact source commit linked in the native package README:
https://github.com/resoltico/HTMLCut/releases

Source archives retain the local dependency sources and their original notices
under patches/. Cargo.lock records exact registry dependency versions; their
source packages are available from https://crates.io/ using those names and
versions. Their licenses remain applicable independently of the project license.

Native distributions must include the complete dependency permission/license
texts and required attributions for their locked build graph, including local
patched dependencies and supplementary copyright notices. Do not treat a
representative crate list or this project-scope notice as a complete dependency
license report.

